{
  "about": "What the workers' disk guards decide on Windows, tested against both: PathGuard (C#) through DiskGuardVectorTests and disk-guard.js through disk-guard.test.js. Each scenario is a made-up disk. 'links' maps a link to the text it holds, as the system reports it. 'aliases' maps a second name for an entry (a short name, or a name Windows trims) to the entry. 'refused' is true or false for both workers, or one answer for each: the C# worker follows no link inside a repository, and the TypeScript worker follows one that leads to a place it would read, as a package manager's links do.",
  "scenarios": [
    {
      "name": "a repository on a drive",
